    "body":  "## What\nAdds the official declarative PagerDuty connector to Switch Core\u0027s service connections catalog.\n\n## Why\nEnables operators and users to connect their PagerDuty account in Switch Console so agents can inspect incidents, check on-call schedules, explore escalation policies, and coordinate incident response in rooms.\n\n## Details\n- Follows the declarative `adapter: api_key` pattern documented in `docs/design/service-connections-v2.md`.\n- **Endpoints:**\n  - US: `https://mcp.pagerduty.com/mcp` and REST `https://api.pagerduty.com/users/me`\n  - EU: `https://mcp.eu.pagerduty.com/mcp` and REST `https://api.eu.pagerduty.com/users/me`\n- **Authentication:** Validates API key against `/users/me` with `Authorization: Token token={api_key}`, extracting `user.id` and `user.email`.\n- **MCP Server:** Passes through to `https://mcp.{region}/mcp` with `Authorization: Token token={api_key}` header.\n- **Skill:** Provides safe operational guidance for incident management and summarizing alert data without exposing credentials.\n- **Console UI:** Includes official Simple Icons `pagerduty.svg` vector icon and attribution in `NOTICE.md`.\n- **Tests:** Full unit test coverage in `test_loader.py` validating schema compliance.\n\nCloses #825",
